.Dd March 28, 2026
.Dt VBSD_COALITION 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm vbsd_coalition
.Nd capability-based resource group management
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/vbsd_coalition.h
.Pp
.Fd #include <sys/ioctl.h>
.Fd #include <fcntl.h>
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
device provides capability-based resource group management for
.Fx .
A coalition groups file descriptors representing capabilities (processes,
jails, sockets, devices, etc.) that should be terminated together when
the coalition is closed.
.Pp
Opening
.Pa /dev/vbsd_coalition
creates a new coalition.
The returned file descriptor represents the authority to terminate all
enlisted members.
Closing the coalition fd terminates all members.
.Ss Enlisting Members
Members are enlisted using
.Xr ioctl 2 :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
int member_fd = /* procdesc, jaildesc, socket, etc. */;
ioctl(coalition_fd, VBSD_COALITION_ENLIST, &member_fd);
.Ed
.Pp
The coalition takes a reference to the file descriptor.
The caller retains their fd and can continue using it.
Enlistment is one-way; members cannot be removed except by coalition
termination.
.Ss Self-Join
A process can join itself to a coalition:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
ioctl(coalition_fd, VBSD_COALITION_JOIN, NULL);
.Ed
.Pp
The process will be terminated when the coalition closes.
.Ss Termination
Termination occurs when:
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
The coalition fd is closed (last reference dropped)
.It
.Dv VBSD_COALITION_TERMINATE
ioctl is called
.It
A deadline or watchdog timer expires
.It
The designated leader dies
.El
.Pp
On termination:
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
Processes receive SIGKILL (or configured signal)
.It
Jails are removed via
.Xr jail_remove 2
.It
Sockets are shut down
.It
Custom devices have their termination callback invoked
.El
.Sh IOCTLS
.Bl -tag -width VBSD_COALITION_TERMINATE_GRACEFUL
.It Dv VBSD_COALITION_ENLIST
Enlist a file descriptor in the coalition.
Argument is a pointer to
.Vt int
containing the fd to enlist.
.It Dv VBSD_COALITION_ENLIST_SET
Enlist multiple file descriptors at once.
Argument is a pointer to
.Vt struct vbsd_enlist_set .
Stops on first error;
.Va enlisted
field returns count of successful enlistments.
.It Dv VBSD_COALITION_JOIN
Self-join: the calling process joins the coalition.
No argument.
.It Dv VBSD_COALITION_TERMINATE
Immediately terminate all coalition members.
No argument.
.It Dv VBSD_COALITION_TERMINATE_GRACEFUL
Send a signal first, then SIGKILL after timeout.
Argument is a pointer to
.Vt struct vbsd_graceful .
.It Dv VBSD_COALITION_STAT
Query coalition status.
Argument is a pointer to
.Vt struct vbsd_coalition_stat .
.It Dv VBSD_COALITION_SET_SIGNAL
Set the termination signal (default SIGKILL).
Argument is a pointer to
.Vt int .
.It Dv VBSD_COALITION_SET_DEADLINE
Set automatic termination after timeout.
Argument is a pointer to
.Vt struct vbsd_deadline .
Set
.Va vd_timeout_ms
to 0 to cancel.
.It Dv VBSD_COALITION_SET_WATCHDOG
Enable watchdog timer requiring periodic heartbeats.
Argument is a pointer to
.Vt uint32_t
containing timeout in milliseconds.
Set to 0 to disable.
.It Dv VBSD_COALITION_HEARTBEAT
Reset the watchdog timer.
No argument.
.It Dv VBSD_COALITION_SET_LEADER
Designate a member as leader; its death triggers coalition termination.
Argument is a pointer to
.Vt int
containing the fd.
Set to -1 to clear.
.It Dv VBSD_COALITION_RUSAGE
Get aggregate resource usage for all process members.
Argument is a pointer to
.Vt struct vbsd_coalition_rusage .
.El
.Sh KQUEUE
Coalition file descriptors support
.Xr kqueue 2
with
.Dv EVFILT_READ .
Events are delivered in
.Va fflags :
.Bl -tag -width VBSD_NOTE_MEMBER_REMOVED -compact
.It Dv VBSD_NOTE_MEMBER_ADDED
New member enlisted
.It Dv VBSD_NOTE_MEMBER_REMOVED
Member exited or removed
.It Dv VBSD_NOTE_TERMINATING
Termination started
.It Dv VBSD_NOTE_TERMINATED
All members terminated
.It Dv VBSD_NOTE_LEADER_DIED
Leader death triggered termination
.It Dv VBSD_NOTE_DEADLINE_FIRED
Deadline timer expired
.It Dv VBSD_NOTE_WATCHDOG_FIRED
Watchdog timeout
.It Dv VBSD_NOTE_GRACE_STARTED
Grace period began
.El
.Sh CAPSICUM
Coalition file descriptors work with
.Xr capsicum 4 .
Use
.Xr cap_ioctls_limit 2
to restrict available ioctls:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
unsigned long cmds[] = { VBSD_COALITION_ENLIST, VBSD_COALITION_STAT };
cap_ioctls_limit(coalition_fd, cmds, nitems(cmds));
.Ed
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /dev/vbsd_coalition
.It Pa /dev/vbsd_coalition
Coalition device node
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Create a coalition and enlist a child process:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
int coalition_fd, proc_fd;
pid_t pid;

coalition_fd = open("/dev/vbsd_coalition", O_RDWR);

pid = pdfork(&proc_fd, 0);
if (pid == 0) {
    /* child */
    execl("/bin/worker", "worker", NULL);
}

/* Enlist child in coalition */
ioctl(coalition_fd, VBSD_COALITION_ENLIST, &proc_fd);

/* ... later ... */
close(coalition_fd);  /* Terminates child */
.Ed
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Bq Er EBUSY
Resource already enlisted in a coalition.
.It Bq Er EINVAL
Coalition is terminating, invalid signal, or invalid leader type.
.It Bq Er EBADF
Invalid file descriptor.
.It Bq Er ESRCH
Process or jail no longer exists, or leader not enlisted.
.It Bq Er ESHUTDOWN
Coalition already terminated.
.It Bq Er ENOMEM
Resource limit exceeded.
.It Bq Er ELOOP
Nesting depth limit exceeded.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr jail 2 ,
.Xr kqueue 2 ,
.Xr pdfork 2 ,
.Xr capsicum 4 ,
.Xr vbsd_coalition 9
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
device first appeared in
.Fx 15.0 .
